"id": "adjectives",
"el": "Τα επίθετα",
"title": "Adjectives and agreement",
"span": "A1–B2",
"part": "Μέρος Γ΄ | Επίθετο και επίρρημα | Adjectives and adverbs",
"blurb": "The adjective types -ος/-η/-ο, -ος/-α/-ο, -ύς/-ιά/-ύ, -ής/-ές and -ης/-α/-ικο, πολύς, colours that never change, and agreement in gender, number and case.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "A Greek adjective agrees with its noun in **gender, number and case**. In practice the adjective usually takes the same ending as the article: **ο καλός φίλος, η καλή φίλη, το καλό παιδί**. Learn the adjective in three forms (masculine, feminine, neuter), as dictionaries give it: **καλός, -ή, -ό**."
},
